Include iphlpapi.h instead of netioapi.h on Windows

netioapi.h is only meant to be included through iphlpapi.h. When it is
included directly, __IPHLPAPI_H__ is not defined and the header takes its
kernel-mode branch, which declares every function with the NTSTATUS type
that does not exist in a user-mode build. With MSVC and the Windows 10 SDK
this fails with:

    netioapi.h(229): error C2143: syntax error: missing '{' before '__cdecl'

iphlpapi.h includes netioapi.h itself, in user mode, and provides
if_nametoindex() the same way.

diff --git a/src/misc.c b/src/misc.c
--- a/src/misc.c
+++ b/src/misc.c
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 #include <ws2tcpip.h>
 #include <shlobj.h>
 #include <direct.h>
-#include <netioapi.h>
+#include <iphlpapi.h>
 
 #ifdef HAVE_IO_H
 #include <io.h>
